  "worked_solution": "Since $A$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, then we can write\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the scale factor and $\\theta $ is the angle of rotation. \n\nAccording to the diagram, $r=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
